{"key":"enterprise/T1055.012","id":"T1055.012","name":"Process Hollowing","domain":"enterprise","level":"subtechnique","parent_id":"T1055","tactics":["privilege-escalation","stealth"],"platforms":["Windows"],"environments":["cloud-hosted-endpoint","onprem"],"environment_basis":"project_taxonomy_from_upstream_platforms","summary":"Adversaries may inject malicious code into suspended and hollowed processes in order to evade process-based defenses. Process hollowing is a method of executing arbitrary code in the address space of a separate live process. Process hollowing is commonly performed by creating a process in a suspended state then unmapping/hollowing its memory, which can then be replaced with malicious code. A victim process can be created with native Windows API…","source_url":"https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1055/012","source_stix_id":"attack-pattern--b200542e-e877-4395-875b-cf1a44537ca4","source_modified":"2026-05-12T15:12:00.708Z","source_object_version":"2.0","telemetry":{"status":"mapped","components":[{"id":"DC0021","name":"OS API Execution","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0021","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--9bde2f9d-a695-4344-bfac-f2dce13d121e","page":"telemetry/DC0021/"},{"id":"DC0035","name":"Process Access","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0035","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--1887a270-576a-4049-84de-ef746b2572d6","page":"telemetry/DC0035/"},{"id":"DC0032","name":"Process Creation","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0032","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--3d20385b-24ef-40e1-9f56-f39750379077","page":"telemetry/DC0032/"},{"id":"DC0020","name":"Process Modification","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0020","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--d5fca4e4-e47a-487b-873f-3d22f8865e96","page":"telemetry/DC0020/"}],"strategies":[{"id":"DET0382","name":"Detection Strategy for Process Hollowing on Windows","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0382","stix_id":"x-mitre-de